listen to geralt speak and see if you  notice anything different  about the way he talks running low on  patience  got some other things on my mind looking  for a woman  recognize me from master dandelion's  balance 2  came to look for you crocs worried  taking you home need to find your friend  could go with a kobold's eyes  but the creatures are sentient rather  not gouge one's eyes out  i've played a ton of the witcher 3 and  cyberpunk 2077.  i've witnessed nearly every possible  outcome in geralt's adventure and i'm  already a hundred hours deep in  cyberpunk 2077.  one thing that's always stood out to me  about cd projekt red's characters is how  they talk  they almost always chop off the  beginning of their sentences  before we get into it make sure to  subscribe to stay up to date on all  things cyberpunk  now let's run that geralt montage again  running low on patience  got some other things on my mind looking  for a woman  recognize me from master dandelion's  ballads too  came to look for you crocs worried  taking you home notice how in every  single one of these scenes  geralt drops the subject pronoun for  those who haven't opened an english  textbook recently like yours truly  subject pronouns are i you he she they  and so on  instead of saying something like i don't  think that's a good idea  geralt says don't think that's a good  idea  back in 2015 when i played the witcher 3  i just chalked it up to the fact that  geralt's a badass and badasses used  their words sparingly  by cutting off the subject pronoun of  most of his sentences  he just sounded well more badass that's  the problem  it was more however when i got my hands  on cyberpunk 2077 i noticed that many  characters also speak like geralt  even keanu reeves character johnny  silverhand  sure hope so b now i think it's safe to  say that johnny is a badass as well but  hearing keanu reeves cut off the  beginning of his sentences  sounded off imagine if john wick said  they cannot  back instead of i'm thinking i'm back  it just doesn't feel right johnny  silverhand isn't the only character in  cyberpunk 2077 that speaks like this  though  nearly every character does didn't  answer my question now  did you looking for evelyn parker know  if you see her  come on no place we can talk where ears  won't prick up to listen  i'm stepping outside can't smoke in here  it doesn't matter who they are where  they come from or what they do  they frequently drop the subject pronoun  at the beginning of their sentences  sure we could pin it all on the fact  that everyone in night city is a badass  and therefore needs to use as few words  as possible but the real reason might be  a bit more complicated than that  this way of speaking is actually common  in the polish language and according to  cyberpunk 2077's quest director whose  name i'm going to butcher matej  tomaskovich  cyberpunk 2077 script was written in  polish  and then translated into english  all right brace yourself for a brief  lesson in verb conjugation  polish is what's known as a pro-drop  language short for pronoun dropping and  is one of the many languages where  subject pronouns like you she  i or they are regularly omitted in the  case of polish verbs are conjugated  according to the subject which often  makes the subject pronoun  redundant in standard english verbs are  mainly conjugated for tense rather than  subject  i played you played she played or i will  play you will play  she will play or they will play i wombo  he she me the main exception is in the  third person present tense you'd say he  plays  rather than he play but generally  speaking you can't  automatically know what the subject of  the sentence is just from the verb form  used  in polish however conjugated verbs match  both the person  first person second person or third  person and the number  singular or plural in other words the  verb form automatically tells you  whether the subject of the sentence is  me we you she he and so on meaning you  don't need the actual pronoun to be  understood  i don't speak polish but i do know some  spanish and it works basically the same  way  so to avoid butchering polish here's  some spanish conjugation to show how  this works  hablar means to talk in spanish as you  can see there's a different form of the  verb  depending on the subject and whether  it's singular or plural  hablo by itself means i talk because of  this you don't need these pronouns  unless you really want to emphasize the  subject  compare that with english where there  are only two ways to conjugate to talk  in the present tense talk or talks  english is not a pro-drop language and  most of the time we do need subject  pronouns in order to make sense  or just to sound natural there are  examples of pronoun dropping in english  though you might say sorry instead of  i'm sorry for something minor or you  might say love you instead of i love you  to certain people  we almost always drop the subject  pronoun you from commands like  clean your room but to drop the subject  pronoun regardless of the situation like  the characters in cyberpunk 2077 do  just sounds unnatural to the  english-speaking ear even if you can  understand from the context what the  character means  what's more interesting is that dying  light is a zombie free-running game  developed by polish studio techland  doesn't do this this is most likely due  to the fact that dying light was written  in collaboration with an american  novelist named dan  jolly here's a scene from the beginning  of dying light  all right taken care of piece of cake  what else you got for me well  let me think raheem you are just smart  enough to be dangerous you know that  omar told me about your plans for the  nest explosive charges  really what explosives okay please say  that  you can't tell a convincing lie to save  your life i know what i'm doing  yeah you think you can't die you're not  my mom no  i'm not our mom's dead so you might want  to be a little nicer to me since i'm the  only family you have left  especially now that amir is gone you're  jade right  right i just wanted to thank you for  what you did for me and tell you how  sorry i am for your loss  i owe you and a mirror in my life yeah  you do you want to return the favor  keep my [ __ ] brother from killing  himself  no explosives raheem as you can see  for most of these sentences the subject  pronoun hasn't been dropped so in  cyberpunk 2077 and the witcher 3 the  dialogue style could be a result of a  more literal translation from polish or  it could very well be a stylistic choice  to make the characters sound cooler or  edgier  is this a good way to write dialogue  though i don't really know  i was taught that punchy natural  sounding dialogue is the way to go  it's simple we uh kill the batman  cutting out words certainly makes  dialogue more punchy but does it sound  natural personally i thought that way of  speaking fit geralt really well  he's a man of few words so dropping the  subject pronoun whenever possible made  sense for his character  even if it wasn't intentional maybe it's  due to the different accents in the  fantasy setting  but generally i only notice when geralt  drops subject pronouns  in cyberpunk's case though i find it  pretty distracting maybe it's because i  was born and raised in california and i  know people don't and  probably won't ever talk like that but  hey you might feel differently if so let  me know in the comments below  and for more cyberpunk 2077 make sure to  subscribe to gamespot  [Music]  so  [Music]  you
 

